{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789784301,"nonce":"KgbQJNFTcrnzM0D7O1l/LMLrFuc=","title":"a subclass of a not-yet-lowered parent lays its fields over the parent's slots","message":"`BytesInput extends Input`: with Input a Placeholder in BytesInput's\ncontext (its file lowers later), `collect_inherited_fields` found no parent\nsymbol and reserved nothing, so BytesInput's `b` took slot 1 — `Input.bigEndian`'s\nslot — and every read through the base class saw big-endian. The\ndeclaration index already counts a class's inherited slots\n(`instance_field_count`); the layout now reserves that many for a\nPlaceholder parent.\n\nAlso on the way: `#elseif` inside an inline conditional (`var b:#if js A\ntext, the RD parser failed the file and the legacy fallback dropped the\nclass; `rayzor.Bytes` gained `new(length, data)` and `getData()` so\n`BytesBuffer.getBytes()` and `BytesInput` work over the `Array\u003cInt\u003e`\nBytesData.\n\nFixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/CrossModuleOverride.hx (the Bytes\nround trip).","files":null}]}